lisa-design:
- R74 SeedPath: rel is the literal relationship policyFile == policyPath + "/" + rel (no Clean/Abs: plugins seed with literal strings). Extension beyond the spec: when policyPath already ends in "/", policyFile == policyPath + rel and the path seed keeps the trailing "/" (so the legacy pair is reproduced for that form too). Empty policyPath / file outside path => no rel => path seed = ID.
- R74 Policy.ID is set only when the evaluated policy_id is a string ValidPolicyID accepts (non-empty, valid UTF-8, <=512 runes). An invalid one never fails Execute; ValidateResult reports invalid-policy-id (error). policy_id stays in AdditionalVariables (unchanged behaviour). Result.String() deliberately unchanged.
- R75 static: policy_id must be one unconditional rule `policy_id := "<literal>"` (no default, no else, no ref head, no resolution through constants). Function/contains definitions keep the generic contract-key-function / contract-key-multi-value codes (policy_id is in contractKeys); everything else is invalid-policy-id. Defining it more than once in a package flags every extra definition and the package's ID is not compared for duplicates.
- R75 duplicate-policy-id is per CheckContract call (regocheck = per inline bundle; playback = per request). Cross-bundle/per-plugin duplicates are the agent's job. Reported on every declaration after the first in file order.
- PolicyCode* constants live in pkg/agentconfig (no OPA import); the two shared with policyeval are asserted equal in a regocheck test. PolicyError.Code is not validated server-side, so no enum was extended.
- R76/R77 storage: plugin-path rides inside the existing policy_bundles jsonb; plugins is a new jsonb column on ccf_agent_instances (AutoMigrate), part of reportColumns (a report without plugins clears it) and summaryColumns (returned in list summaries and details as `plugins`, [] when absent). Limits: <=500 plugins (truncated, sets truncated), name<=255/source<=2048/lib-version<=64 bytes UTF-8-truncated, empty name => 400; plugin-path >4096 bytes is dropped (not cut, since a cut path would yield a wrong policy_id) and sets truncated.
- Merge of #466: evidence playback gains top-level `issues` (CheckContract over stored modules) and `replay.issues` (ValidateResult), always [] when nothing / when the replay cannot run; contractIssues now takes EvaluateModulesRequest.Modules.

